---
code: K0008
title: If Without Else
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [ parse, syntax, control-flow, expression ]
description: "'if' expression is missing a required 'else' branch"
---

In Kura, `if` is an expression that always evaluates to a value, so every `if` branch must have a matching `else` branch.

## Example

This error occurs when an `if` expression is written without a fallback `else` clause:

```kura
let label = if is_active {
  "Active"
}
```

It also occurs inside view blocks when conditional rendering omits the `else` branch:

```kura
view {
  if show_banner {
    Text("Welcome!")
  }
}
```

## Solution

Provide an `else` branch that evaluates to a compatible type:

```kura
let label = if is_active {
  "Active"
} else {
  "Inactive"
}
```

Inside UI view blocks where nothing should be rendered when the condition is false, return an empty block or `none` in the `else` branch:

```kura
view {
  if show_banner {
    Text("Welcome!")
  } else {
    none
  }
}
```
